00:28:30.880 --> 00:28:31.800
They just like this movie.

00:28:31.880 --> 00:28:32.920
It didn't start with Part 2.

00:28:32.940 --> 00:28:37.460
This one finally decided, though, that it's important to include the title of the movie in

00:28:37.460 --> 00:28:39.840
full. The other ones were just Rambo and Rambo.

00:28:40.100 --> 00:28:41.960
This one finally includes the title.

00:28:41.960 --> 00:28:48.620
And this is an overhead action shoot-em-up like Commando and Ikari Warriors.

00:28:49.240 --> 00:28:54.540
So, again, sounds normal and sounds like what I was imagining the NES game was going to

00:28:54.540 --> 00:28:56.820
be. Yeah. Apparently very uninspired.

00:28:57.360 --> 00:28:58.660
Okay. Like the rest of them.

00:28:59.040 --> 00:29:06.840
Then we have Rambo the video game, which was an arcade rail shooter video game for PS3

00:29:06.840 --> 00:29:07.940
and 360.

00:29:08.400 --> 00:29:10.940
Could you tell which one it was based on?

00:29:11.120 --> 00:29:14.660
Yeah. No, I think this was like a standalone story.

00:29:14.900 --> 00:29:17.020
Oh. You know, like you're just playing as Rambo.

00:29:17.040 --> 00:29:18.320
This is the next chapter of Rambo.

00:29:18.480 --> 00:29:24.200
Yeah. But this one, it's interesting because there's a lot of things going on here.

00:29:24.200 --> 00:29:28.780
But at the same time, it's an on-rails shooter with Rambo.

00:29:28.880 --> 00:29:33.300
And it's almost like, you know, in the 360 time, like you could have easily have made like

00:29:33.300 --> 00:29:34.440
an explorable area.

00:29:34.620 --> 00:29:35.600
Like you could have just almost...

00:29:35.600 --> 00:29:40.880
Open world Rambo. I don't need open world, but I would have liked like some kind of like Tomb Raider-esque

00:29:40.880 --> 00:29:42.720
Rambo in Vietnam.

00:29:43.880 --> 00:29:47.560
Instead, you just have to do whatever the game directs towards you.

00:29:48.340 --> 00:29:51.540
And then the last one we have here is Rambo.

00:29:51.800 --> 00:29:54.720
The 2008 arcade game.

00:29:54.900 --> 00:29:59.580
It was a light gun shooter developed by Sega for the arcades.

00:29:59.780 --> 00:30:04.520
And it's based on Rambo First Blood Part 2 and Rambo 3.

00:30:04.960 --> 00:30:10.300
Oh. Rambo 3, it's worth noting, came out in 1988.

00:30:10.860 --> 00:30:16.220
So I believe that this Rambo game, based on the story of Rambo First Blood Part 2 for

00:30:16.220 --> 00:30:20.120
the NES, might have been done to kind of like hype up Rambo 3 for people.

00:30:20.620 --> 00:30:22.420
You know, like, oh, let's get this game out.

00:30:22.840 --> 00:30:24.160
Yeah. Get people excited.

00:30:24.480 --> 00:30:26.980
But there's not going to be a Rambo 3 game for the NES.

00:30:27.100 --> 00:30:29.080
There's not going to be any more Rambo games for the NES.

00:30:29.240 --> 00:30:30.420
This is the Rambo game.

00:30:30.480 --> 00:30:34.800
So how do you feel knowing that this is the only chance you'll get at Rambo?

00:30:35.240 --> 00:30:37.180
I'm totally okay with that.

00:30:37.400 --> 00:30:41.300
Great. We'll discuss this further on the Essential Games list.

00:30:43.800 --> 00:30:47.440
Sean, you said you were okay, but are you?

00:30:47.580 --> 00:30:50.200
Right now I'm a little sick, Mike, but I appreciate the thought.

00:30:50.300 --> 00:31:01.740
Thank you for telling us. Anyway, this game, I like the idea of more in-depth stories in these games.

00:31:01.740 --> 00:31:09.460
I like the idea of a good adaptation within a video game release.

00:31:10.440 --> 00:31:20.500
I don't think that this was the correct medium, the correct genre, or the correct property to do this kind of game.

00:31:22.220 --> 00:31:30.520
Even if it were well done, like, even if the story beats made sense within the game, the gameplay itself is just too jank.

00:31:30.860 --> 00:31:35.800
Like, the one thing we didn't really touch on is just the act of using your knife.

00:31:35.960 --> 00:31:37.940
It just feels wrong.

00:31:38.120 --> 00:31:41.200
It feels like there's this weird delay while you get out your knife.

00:31:41.200 --> 00:31:45.360
And that meant that I couldn't hit anything without getting hit first.

00:31:45.660 --> 00:31:48.720
So that just put a bad taste in my mouth of the rest of the game.

00:31:49.600 --> 00:31:52.180
Obviously, I said I didn't really get very far in it.

00:31:52.280 --> 00:31:54.960
So I'm just going to call this one an Essential.

00:31:56.620 --> 00:31:57.500
Not Essential.

00:31:57.880 --> 00:31:59.400
There we go. All right.

00:31:59.580 --> 00:32:09.260
Joe? So I feel like they really tried to, like, have – they had these really cool ideas, but I just feel like they didn't put enough into each of these ideas to make them work.

00:32:09.420 --> 00:32:19.980
Like, they were like – it was like the beginning of the ideas were there, but they didn't build the game in a way that it supports those ideas of, like, the – I keep saying those ideas, but I mean those mechanics.

00:32:21.220 --> 00:32:27.540
And for that reason, and for really all the reasons Sean said as well, I'm going to say also not Essential.

00:32:28.440 --> 00:32:34.420
Yeah, I mean I think it's very clear Rambo on the NES has not been remembered by many people.

00:32:34.740 --> 00:32:38.240
And I actually thought it was surprising to find this, like, Zelda 2 link to it.

00:32:38.960 --> 00:32:49.460
Link. But, like, for everything that's, like, cool about that, like, tidbit, nothing about, like, even describing that to me.

00:32:49.540 --> 00:32:51.320
It's like, oh, yeah, yeah, yeah. You ever play this Rambo game?

00:32:51.340 --> 00:32:52.320
It's like Zelda 2.

00:32:52.460 --> 00:32:55.680
Like, you play as Sylvester Stallone and you're free in prisoners of war in Vietnam.

00:32:55.680 --> 00:32:59.100
I'm not like, oh, well, I have to get a hold of that, you know?

00:32:59.220 --> 00:33:07.860
Like, even the description alone, as cool as the, like, fact that an action movie got that kind of, like, treatment on the NES, it's like, nah, I think I'll pass.

00:33:08.020 --> 00:33:09.880
And that's exactly what wound up happening.

00:33:10.060 --> 00:33:18.140
And, yes, it's for a lot of the shortcomings of the mechanics and, you know, combat wasn't especially enjoyable by any means.

00:33:18.140 --> 00:33:25.740
I think overall this game just kind of is really only for, like, fans of that movie at this time.

00:33:26.160 --> 00:33:30.080
Like, even now, fans of the Rambo movies would be better off probably.

00:33:30.080 --> 00:33:36.080
I mean, I haven't even played it, but you'd be better off playing the Rambo arcade rail shooter for the 360 PS3.

00:33:36.080 --> 00:33:44.740
Like, this game was a product of its time and it just has enough setbacks there that, like, just leave it not essential.

00:33:45.020 --> 00:33:55.460
One thing I will say, though, and I know that even without the prior knowledge of knowing that Zelda 2 doesn't have the best reputation,

00:33:56.420 --> 00:33:59.420
I'm not looking forward to that if that's what this game is like.

00:33:59.420 --> 00:34:00.340
Got it, yeah.

00:34:00.440 --> 00:34:10.060
It's important to note, a lot of people do think that Zelda 2 has been cheated and, like, stepped on by the wrong people and, like, it just needs its day in the sunlight.

00:34:10.380 --> 00:34:14.660
You know, like, if only people would play it, they would understand that it's actually good.

00:34:14.820 --> 00:34:16.540
Just because it's different doesn't mean it's bad.

00:34:16.740 --> 00:34:18.000
Now people are, like, all the, yeah.

00:34:18.180 --> 00:34:19.760
This is how Zelda games work, by the way.

00:34:19.960 --> 00:34:23.140
Like, the newest Zelda game is the best Zelda game.

00:34:23.260 --> 00:34:26.000
And then a year later, it's the worst Zelda game.

00:34:26.160 --> 00:34:27.100
Like Breath of the Wild, right?

00:34:27.100 --> 00:34:30.520
Right, right. It's like, oh, yeah, Breath of the Wild, like, you thought that was good?

